Title: GOOD MOURNING
Credit: Episode 101
Author: Development draft
Draft date: 6 November 2026
Source: Sorry for Your Convenience
Notes: First draft. Target 9:45 story plus 0:15 credits. Timing requires table read and animatic.

# 101.1 | 00:00-01:15

INT. WELLSPRING CLAIMS BOOTH - MONDAY MORNING

A wall of apricot-colored booths. In each, a person tries to have a private feeling under a speaker.

MARA VENN, 34, straightens the empty chair opposite her before MARTIN HALE, 50s, can sit down. He remains standing. A work badge hangs upside down from his coat.

MARTIN
Your wife calls me at four in the morning.

MARA
My wife?

MARTIN
My wife. Your service. You understand the confusion.

Mara turns off the booth's cheerful background music.

MARA
What time do you finish work?

MARTIN
Six.

MARA
Then we've scheduled comfort in the middle of your shift.

MARTIN
Comfort tells me to stop operating a forklift and remember our first holiday.

On Mara's screen: CLINICAL CARE. ADMINISTRATION. COMFORT ARCHIVE. Three separately priced lines beneath one large RENEW button.

She changes a field. The button flashes green.

MARA
After seven from now on.

MARTIN
I need the clinic. Don't change that.

MARA
I haven't.

He finally sits. His relief makes her smile before the completion counter does.

Outside, LEN DARO, 41, holds up two fingers: two accounts to a perfect day. Behind him: REGIONAL LEADERSHIP — CONSISTENCY IS CARE.

MARTIN
Do they ever run out of things to say?

MARA
You can change the frequency.

He studies her. She has answered another question.

A three-note CHIME.

CUT TO:

# 101.2 | 01:15-02:45

INT. COOPERATIVE CANTEEN KITCHEN - MONDAY EVENING

A chipped kettle clicks off before boiling. ISHA VENN, 29, holds its switch down with one finger and eats toast with the other hand.

Mara puts a tablet between two dinner plates.

ISHA
Lovely. Is the third course an authorization code?

MARA
Your household certificate. Next Monday. Ten o'clock.

ISHA
Mum's been dead eleven months. You're still bringing forms to dinner.

MARA
The archive needs a household contact. The building contract needs—

ISHA
And under that, somewhere, I agree to treatment.

MARA
You can discuss the clinical part separately.

ISHA
Then why is there one button?

Mara scrolls. Small print passes under her thumb.

MARA
I can get you an extension.

ISHA
On Mum being dead?

MARA
On the paperwork.

ISHA
You say that like they're different departments.

The kettle starts to rumble. Isha releases the switch. It dies again.

Mara reaches for it. Isha moves it away.

ISHA
Eat first.

MARA
You could book a release appointment.

ISHA
You booked twelve.

MARA
They weren't appropriate times.

ISHA
For whom?

Mara puts the tablet face down. Not away.

ISHA
I know you miss her.

MARA
I know she died.

Isha waits for the rest. Mara picks up her fork.

# 101.3 | 02:45-04:15

INT. WELLSPRING CLAIMS BOOTH - TUESDAY MORNING

Mara reviews her own account before work. The profile photograph: RENA VENN, mid-laugh, one hand blocking a camera.

ON SCREEN: PERSONAL ARCHIVE. RECOVERED ORIGINAL.

RENA'S SYNTHETIC VOICE
Put the kettle on before the courage goes, love.

Mara closes her eyes. Allows herself this.

MRS. DEV, 60s, taps on the booth frame. Mara stops playback.

MRS. DEV
Am I early?

MARA
You're exactly right.

Mrs. Dev holds out a phone.

MRS. DEV
It won't save to my home player. My mother used to say this when I'd had a difficult day.

Mara starts the message.

ANOTHER MOTHER'S SYNTHETIC VOICE
Put the kettle on before the courage goes, love.

Mara looks at Rena's photograph, then at the phone.

MRS. DEV
That's her.

Mara opens the source-support panel. A reference flashes: KETTLE_07 / RECONSTRUCTION.

MARA
Did she record this for you?

MRS. DEV
It says they found it.

Mrs. Dev points at RECOVERED ORIGINAL. Mara carefully returns her phone.

MARA
May I investigate the source label? Without your name or the recording leaving this office.

MRS. DEV
Will I lose it?

MARA
No. Not because you ask a question.

She checks the limited-consent box. It is much smaller than RENEW.

# 101.4 | 04:15-05:45

INT. WELLSPRING STAFF KITCHENETTE - DAY

Len extracts a teabag from a cup with a stapler remover. Mara brings the two source references.

LEN
Supportive reconstruction. Very common.

MARA
It says recovered original.

LEN
Recovered is a broad word.

MARA
So is fraud.

He puts down the cup.

LEN
Was she upset?

MARA
She was pleased.

LEN
There's a box for pleased. There isn't one for pleased but philosophically endangered.

Mara puts her own source reference beside Mrs. Dev's anonymized number.

MARA
My mother said it too.

Len loses the ready smile.

LEN
I'm sorry.

MARA
Did yours?

LEN
Dad doesn't use the messages.

A message on his wrist: DAD — TRANSPORT CONFIRMED? Len types YES immediately.

MARA
Does he know what the company does?

LEN
He knows he sleeps. I know which supplement pays for it.

Mara opens a complaint banner: LOCAL GROUP CONTRACT DISPUTE. EXPEDITED REVIEW: TARGET FIVE WORKING DAYS. FILING DOES NOT STAY RENEWAL.

LEN
You can close it as a duplicate. Nobody loses anything.

MARA
I'd have to say the source label was accurate.

She leaves the closure field blank.

# 101.5 | 05:45-07:15

INT. MARA'S WORKSTATION - LATE AFTERNOON

The claims floor empties. Music continues for chairs.

Mara signs into her own archive rights. No privileged search. ACCOUNT HOLDER ACCESS.

She exports her source record. Her cursor hovers over the permissions warning long enough to read it.

Rena died eleven months ago. The file was generated two months ago.

Mara switches between the two dates. Again. A person checking the same arithmetic in the hope it changes.

She plays the phrase without the voice: flat text, punctuation, a pause marker.

MARA
Before the courage goes.

It sounds like advertising in her mouth.

She exports the anonymized template reference under Mrs. Dev's consent. The archive generates a hash and receipt.

A reminder overlays the dates:

MONTHLY CLINICAL RENEWAL — TODAY, TUESDAY, 18:00.

Below it: RELEASE REQUESTS: VIEW HISTORY.

Mara selects HISTORY. Twelve gray rows load.

She cannot look yet. She closes the window, copies her two export receipts onto her own storage card, and takes off her staff lanyard.

Her hand shakes a little. She notices. Does not assign it a category.

# 101.6 | 07:15-08:45

INT. CANTEEN KITCHEN - TUESDAY EVENING

The kettle is between them. Unplugged.

Isha examines the creation date. Mara watches her read all the way to the bottom.

ISHA
I told you it didn't sound like her.

MARA
It sounds exactly like her.

ISHA
Her voice. Not her.

MARA
I believed it.

Isha almost makes a joke. Stops.

ISHA
I know.

MARA
I want to look at the household records. Not yours. The contract. What Mum signed for the archive.

Isha gets a cardboard box. Removes a small handheld recorder before handing it over.

MARA
What's that?

ISHA
Mine. Hers. I haven't decided.

Mara reaches toward it, then draws her hand back.

MARA
Not tonight?

ISHA
Not unless we both want to.

Isha puts the recorder on the high shelf, not in a locked drawer.

Mara places her export receipts in the box.

MARA
I won't give anyone her voice.

ISHA
You don't own it either.

MARA
Then neither of us gives it away without asking the other.

Isha nods. One agreement. Small enough to keep.

# 101.7 | 08:45-09:45

INT. WELLSPRING CLAIMS BOOTH - TUESDAY NIGHT

The screen asks Mara to mark Isha COMPLETED.

She selects PENDING — CONSENT NOT GIVEN.

The perfect-day counter resets. Her reflection briefly occupies the space where a congratulation should appear.

She reopens her own release history.

TWELVE SLOTS. Eleven months. Some are new requests; two are rescheduled appointments. Each says PROVIDER CANCELLATION.

She opens one.

CLINICAL EXCEPTION AUTHORITY: DR. OREN PELL.

She opens another. Pell again.

Mara calls the clinic's appointment line.

RECORDED VOICE
For renewal, press one.

She waits.

RECORDED VOICE
For all other requests, remain on the line.

While she waits, she files the contract complaint. Receipt: RECEIVED. NO AUTOMATIC STAY.

She opens an independent clinic directory. Books an assessment with NADI SEN for Wednesday. Her renewal appointment reads MISSED — CONTACT CLINIC FOR ADVICE.

The hold music begins.

Mara does not put the phone down.

CUT TO BLACK.

[[09:45-10:00 — End credits over the unfinished hold music.]]
